AO3.3
Minimum setbacks are in accordance with the following:
- carports and garages are set back a minimum of six (6) metres from all road frontages;
- building walls are set back a minimum of three (3) metres from all road frontages;
- verandahs are set back a minimum of one (1) metre from all road frontages;
- the rear boundary setback is four (4) metres unless to a laneway being one (1) metre at ground storey and 0.5 metres above ground level;
- garages and open car ports built along the side boundary do not exceed a length of nine (9) metres.
Editor’s note—Side setbacks for a dual occupancy is regulated by the Queensland Development Code MP1.3 unless adjoining an industrial zone or a lawfully operating industrial use – refer to AO4.2.

